          SOURCE=$SPELL-$VERSION.tar.gz
     SOURCE_HASH=sha512:350451669a7195d854ad01f734079301c6b833e9666442d1a8217d0ff33fc29365265dd7112f23b482823065fc48602b27ca300926afa27777d925672ff21c5d
SOURCE_DIRECTORY=$BUILD_DIRECTORY/$SPELL-$VERSION
        WEB_SITE=https://github.com/containers/fuse-overlayfs
   SOURCE_URL[0]=$WEB_SITE/archive/refs/tags/v$VERSION.tar.gz
      LICENSE[0]=GPL
         ENTERED=20261001
        KEYWORDS="filesystem disk"
           SHORT="FUSE overlay filesystem driver"
cat << EOF
FUSE overlay filesystem driver. It combines two or more directory trees
into one, behaving like a union mount, but without requiring privileges:
an unprivileged user can run it inside a user namespace and keep the
lower and upper layers owned by different users.

The kernel union mount cannot express this case, which is what container
runtimes need when they build a root filesystem out of an image layer and
the writes collected on top of it.
EOF
